cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use CallForge, please cite it as below."
title: "CallForge: a targeted-capture germline analysis pipeline (FASTQ -> annotated joint callset -> burden)"
abstract: >-
  CallForge is a disease- and organism-agnostic Nextflow DSL2 pipeline that takes
  demultiplexed paired-end FASTQs from a hybridization-capture panel and produces a
  high-quality, joint-genotyped, annotated, QC'd callset spanning SNV/indel, CNV, STR
  and paralog-aware variants, then a rare-variant burden/association layer. It is the
  analysis counterpart to the CaptureForge probe-design pipeline and consumes its
  handoff (final_covered_targets.bed and per-gene metadata).
authors:
  - family-names: "Adu"
    given-names: "Bright"
    alias: "aduton1000"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3622-2137"
    affiliation: "Genomics & Bioinformatics Core, Noguchi Memorial Institute for Medical Research, University of Ghana, Legon, Ghana"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-06-13"
license: MIT
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/aduton1000/callforge"
keywords:
  - bioinformatics
  - germline variant calling
  - targeted capture
  - joint genotyping
  - GATK
  - rare-variant burden
  - nextflow
references:
  - type: software
    title: "CaptureForge: a general-purpose, organism-agnostic hybridization-capture probe (bait) design pipeline"
    repository-code: "https://github.com/aduton1000/captureforge"
    notes: "Upstream design pipeline; CallForge consumes its final_covered_targets.bed and per-gene metadata."
  - type: software
    title: "FamilyForge: pedigree-aware Mendelian and ACMG-style interpretation of a family callset"
    repository-code: "https://github.com/aduton1000/familyforge"
    notes: "Downstream interpretation layer; consumes CallForge's annotated joint VCF, cnv_calls.tsv and provenance.json."
